1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,148
Across six major Buy Now,

2
00:00:02,148 --> 00:00:05,242
Pay Later firms tracked by the CFPB,

3
00:00:05,242 --> 00:00:08,508
53.6 million borrowers took an average

4
00:00:08,508 --> 00:00:10,570
of 6.3 loans in a single

5
00:00:10,570 --> 00:00:11,000
year.

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,938
In CFPB credit-panel data,

7
00:00:12,938 --> 00:00:15,547
62.7 percent of users held multiple

8
00:00:15,547 --> 00:00:16,964
BNPL loans at once,

9
00:00:16,964 --> 00:00:19,722
and 32.6 percent stacked loans across

10
00:00:19,722 --> 00:00:20,840
different apps.

11
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:23,125
Figure 5 shows active Pay-in-4 loans

12
00:00:23,125 --> 00:00:25,663
spiking every holiday season as separate

13
00:00:25,663 --> 00:00:27,821
biweekly debits pile onto the same

14
00:00:27,821 --> 00:00:28,900
checking account.

15
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:32,020
BNPL borrowers also carried higher credit card,

16
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:32,485
retail,

17
00:00:32,485 --> 00:00:34,277
and personal loan balances,

18
00:00:34,277 --> 00:00:36,535
though the CFPB notes that pattern

19
00:00:36,535 --> 00:00:37,531
is correlation,

20
00:00:37,531 --> 00:00:38,460
not causation.

21
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:40,898
Zero interest is still real debt.

22
00:00:40,898 --> 00:00:43,336
Never open a second Pay-in-4 plan

23
00:00:43,336 --> 00:00:46,070
until your current balance hits zero.
